---
code: K0007
title: Binary Minus Spacing
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [ parse, syntax, operator, whitespace ]
description: "Binary '-' operator requires whitespace on both sides"
---

The binary subtraction operator `-` requires whitespace on both sides to distinguish it from unary negation and negative numeric or unit literals (such as `-10` or `-4px`).

## Example

This error occurs when `-` is placed immediately adjacent to one or both operands in a binary expression:

```kura
let width = 100px-20px
```

It also occurs when whitespace is present on only one side of `-`:

```kura
let offset = x -10
let total = a- b
```

## Solution

Add whitespace on both sides of `-` when performing subtraction:

```kura
let width = 100px - 20px
let offset = x - 10
let total = a - b
```

If you intended to negate a value or pass a negative argument rather than subtract, ensure `-` is only attached to the right-hand operand with whitespace before it (or wrapped in parentheses):

```kura
let negative = -10px
let result = compute(-10)
```
